  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nAlmost always used with {顔|かお} or {眉|まゆ} as the direct object:\n- {顔|かお}をしかめる: to grimace, to make a face\n- {眉|まゆ}をしかめる: to furrow one's brows, to frown\n\nWHAT IT EXPRESSES:\n- {痛|いた}み: pain\n- {不快感|ふかいかん}: displeasure, disgust\n- {困惑|こんわく}: bewilderment\n- {集中|しゅうちゅう}: deep concentration\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{顔|かお}をしかめている describes the ongoing state of having a grimace on one's face.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {眉間|みけん}にしわを{寄|よ}せる: to furrow one's brow (similar, slightly more literary)\n- {渋|しぶ}い{顔|かお}をする: to make a sour face\n- にらむ: to glare (more aggressive)",
